            "body": "Do surfaces jab ek-doosre ko chhoo rahe hon aur ek-doosre par **sarakne** ki koshish karein (ya sarak rahe hon), to unke beech ek force lagta hai jo us sarakne ka **virodh** karta hai. Isi ko **friction** kehte hain.\n\n> **Friction ki disha hamesha us \"relative motion\" ya \"motion ki koshish\" ke ulti hoti hai.**\n\nMaan lo ek kitaab mez par daayein sarak rahi hai. Friction **baayein** lagega, yani kitaab ko rokne ki taraf.\n\n```\n          kitaab -->  (chal rahi hai daayein)\n        +-----------+\n  <-----|  KITAAB   |\n friction +----------+\n ======================  mez\n```\n\n> **Figure 4.1** – Kitaab daayein sarak rahi hai, friction baayein (ulti disha mein) lagta hai.\n\n### Friction hota kyun hai?\n\nSurface chahe kitna bhi chikna dikhe, **koi bhi surface poori tarah smooth nahi hota.** Microscope se dekho to har surface par chhote-chhote ubhaar aur gaddhe (bumps aur dents) hote hain. Jab do surface ek-doosre par rakhe jaate hain, to inke ubhaar ek-doosre ke gaddhon mein **phans** jaate hain. Sarakne ki koshish karne par ye ubhaar ek-doosre ko rokte hain. Wahi rok friction hai.\n\nNeeche do surfaces ka bada kiya hua (zoomed) sketch hai:\n\n```\n   upar wala surface (zoom kiya hua)\n    \\/\\/\\/\\/\\/\\/\\/\\/\\/\\/\\/\\/\n    /\\/\\/\\/\\/\\/\\/\\/\\/\\/\\/\\/\\\n   ------------------------------\n    ubhaar ek-doosre ke gaddhon mein phanse hain\n   ------------------------------\n    \\/\\/\\/\\/\\/\\/\\/\\/\\/\\/\\/\\/\n    /\\/\\/\\/\\/\\/\\/\\/\\/\\/\\/\\/\\\n   neeche wala surface (zoom kiya hua)\n```\n\n> **Figure 4.2** – Do surfaces ka bada kiya hua rup: dono par tiny ubhaar aur gaddhe hote hain, jo ek-doosre mein phans kar sarakne ka virodh karte hain.\n\nIsi wajah se **jitna rough surface, utna zyada friction**, aur jitna smooth surface, utna kam friction.\n\nAur yaad rakho: friction ek **force** hai, isliye iska unit bhi force wala hai: **newton (N)**.",
            "bodyHinglish": "Do surfaces jab ek-doosre ko chhoo rahe hon aur ek-doosre par **sarakne** ki koshish karein (ya sarak rahe hon), to unke beech ek force lagta hai jo us sarakne ka **virodh** karta hai. Isi ko **friction** kehte hain.\n\n> **Friction ki disha hamesha us \"relative motion\" ya \"motion ki koshish\" ke ulti hoti hai.**\n\nMaan lo ek kitaab mez par daayein sarak rahi hai. Friction **baayein** lagega, yani kitaab ko rokne ki taraf.\n\n```\n          kitaab -->  (chal rahi hai daayein)\n        +-----------+\n  <-----|  KITAAB   |\n friction +----------+\n ======================  mez\n```\n\n> **Figure 4.1** – Kitaab daayein sarak rahi hai, friction baayein (ulti disha mein) lagta hai.\n\n### Friction hota kyun hai?\n\nSurface chahe kitna bhi chikna dikhe, **koi bhi surface poori tarah smooth nahi hota.** Microscope se dekho to har surface par chhote-chhote ubhaar aur gaddhe (bumps aur dents) hote hain. Jab do surface ek-doosre par rakhe jaate hain, to inke ubhaar ek-doosre ke gaddhon mein **phans** jaate hain. Sarakne ki koshish karne par ye ubhaar ek-doosre ko rokte hain. Wahi rok friction hai.\n\nNeeche do surfaces ka bada kiya hua (zoomed) sketch hai:\n\n```\n   upar wala surface (zoom kiya hua)\n    \\/\\/\\/\\/\\/\\/\\/\\/\\/\\/\\/\\/\n    /\\/\\/\\/\\/\\/\\/\\/\\/\\/\\/\\/\\\n   ------------------------------\n    ubhaar ek-doosre ke gaddhon mein phanse hain\n   ------------------------------\n    \\/\\/\\/\\/\\/\\/\\/\\/\\/\\/\\/\\/\n    /\\/\\/\\/\\/\\/\\/\\/\\/\\/\\/\\/\\\n   neeche wala surface (zoom kiya hua)\n```\n\n> **Figure 4.2** – Do surfaces ka bada kiya hua rup: dono par tiny ubhaar aur gaddhe hote hain, jo ek-doosre mein phans kar sarakne ka virodh karte hain.\n\nIsi wajah se **jitna rough surface, utna zyada friction**, aur jitna smooth surface, utna kam friction.\n\nAur yaad rakho: friction ek **force** hai, isliye iska unit bhi force wala hai: **newton (N)**."
