            "heading": "Part E: Tides: samundar ka upar-neeche hona",
            "headingHinglish": "Part E: Tides: samundar ka upar-neeche hona",
            "body": "Ab Elisha ke pehle sawaal par aate hain. Samundar ka paani din mein do baar upar chadhta aur do baar utarta hai.\n\n- **High tide:** jab paani kinare par sabse upar tak aata hai.\n- **Low tide:** jab paani sabse peeche chala jaata hai aur retai ka bahut hissa khul jaata hai.\n\nTide koi \"lahar\" (wave) nahi hai. Lahar to hawa se bani chhoti chhoti hilne wali uthal-puthal hai. Tide **paani ke poore level ka dheere dheere (ghanto mein) upar-neeche hona** hai.\n\n### Chaand ki gravity\n\nChaand ki gravity Earth ke samundar ke paani ko bhi kheenchti hai. Chaand ki gravity us taraf ke paani par **thodi zyada** hoti hai jo taraf Chaand ki taraf hai, kyunki wo paani Chaand ke **zyada paas** hai (Topic 2: doori kam, to force zyada). Isliye us taraf ka paani thoda upar uth jaata hai, ek **bulge** ban jaata hai, aur wahan **high tide** aati hai. Jaise Earth ghoomti hai, kinare ke shehar kabhi is bulge ke neeche aate hain, kabhi nahi.\n\nSooraj ki gravity bhi samundar par kaam karti hai, par Sooraj bahut door hai, isliye uska asar Chaand ke asar se **kam** hai (lagbhag aadhe se bhi kam). Dono milkar tide banate hain, aur tide mein Chaand ka role bada hota hai. Isliye \"tide sirf Sooraj ki wajah se aati hai\" galat hai.\n\n### Do bulge kyun, ek nahi?\n\nAap soch sakte ho ki bulge sirf Chaand wali taraf hona chahiye. Par asal mein **do bulge** bante hain: ek Chaand ki taraf, aur ek Earth ke **doosri taraf** (Chaand se ulti disha mein). Isi liye din mein do baar high tide aati hai. Ye ulte taraf wala bulge kyun banta hai, iski **poori wajah aage ki class mein** aayegi. Abhi bas itna jaan lo ki Earth ke dono taraf paani ka ubhaar banta hai, aur Earth apni dhuri par ghoomti hai.\n\n```\n                        low tide\n                  . - - - - - - - - .\n            . '       .---------.       ' .\n   high    (         (   Earth   )         )    high          Chaand\n   tide     ' .       '---------'       . '     tide           ( )\n                  ' - - - - - - - - '\n                        low tide\n\n Bahar ka lamba ghera = samundar ka paani. Chaand ki taraf (daayein) aur\n uski ulti taraf (baayein) paani ubhra hua: do bulge, high tide.\n Upar aur neeche ke hisse mein paani kam: low tide.\n```\n\n> **Figure 6.3** – Earth ke aas-paas samundar ke paani mein do bulge bante hain: ek Chaand ki taraf, ek uski ulti taraf. Jab Earth ghoomte hue kisi shehar ko bulge ke neeche le jaati hai, wahan high tide hoti hai; bulge ke beech wale ilaake mein low tide hoti hai.\n\n### Din mein do tides: waqt\n\nEk jagah par ek high tide se agli high tide tak lagbhag **12 ghante 25 minute** lagte hain. Isliye din mein lagbhag do high tides aur do low tides aati hain. Kyunki 12 h 25 min ka do guna 24 h 50 min hota hai, har din ki tide pichle din se lagbhag 50 minute **der se** aati hai. (Aisa isliye ki Chaand bhi Earth ke chaaro taraf ghoom raha hai, par ye bhi aage ki class mein.)\n\n### Spring tide aur neap tide\n\nTide kabhi bahut badi hoti hai aur kabhi chhoti.\n\n- **Spring tide:** **Poornima** (full moon) aur **amavasya** (new moon) ke din Sooraj, Earth aur Chaand lagbhag **ek seedhi line mein** hote hain. Chaand aur Sooraj dono ka asar ek hi disha mein judta hai, to high tide bahut oonchi aur low tide bahut neeche hoti hai.\n- **Neap tide:** **Aadhe Chaand** (half moon, ashtami ke aas paas) ke din Chaand aur Sooraj Earth se lagbhag sahi-kone (90°) par hote hain. Unka asar ek doosre ko thoda kaat deta hai, to tide chhoti hoti hai: high tide kam oonchi, low tide kam neeche.\n\n```\n  Spring tide (seedhi line)            Neap tide (sahi-kone par)\n\n   Sooraj ---- Earth ---- Chaand        Chaand\n   (ya Chaand ---- Earth ---- Sooraj)      |\n                                           |\n   Dono ka asar jud jaata hai          Earth ------- Sooraj\n   -> bahut badi tide                  Asar ek-doosre ko kaat dete hain\n                                       -> chhoti tide\n```\n\n> **Figure 6.4** – Spring tide: Sooraj, Earth aur Chaand ek seedhi line mein (poornima ya amavasya). Neap tide: Chaand aur Sooraj Earth se sahi-kone par (aadha Chaand).\n\n### Machhuaare aur tide table\n\nMr. Pereira jaise machhuaare aur naav chalane wale **tide table** dekhte hain: kisi bandargaah (port) ke liye har din ki high tide aur low tide ka waqt pehle se likha hota hai. Isse wo tay karte hain ki kab naav samundar mein utaarni hai, kab bandargaah mein ghusna safe hai, aur kab kinare ki retai par kaam karna hai.",
