            "heading": "Introduction",
            "headingHinglish": "Introduction",
            "body": "Pichhle topic mein humne dekha ki sound ki duniya hamare sunne se kaafi badi hai. Insaan lagbhag 20 Hz se 20 kHz tak ki awaaz sun sakta hai (audible range). Usse zyada frequency wali ultrasound ko hum sun nahi paate, par chamgadad aur dolphin use sun lete hain, aur SONAR jaisi machines usse doori naapti hain. Usse kam frequency wali infrasound bhi hamare kaanon ke liye nahi hai. Topic 6 ke ant mein humne kaha tha: jo awaaz sunai nahi deti, wo bhi sound hoti hai aur uske echoes se tasveer ban sakti hai: yahi sonography ka raaz hai.\n\nAb ek sawaal bacha hai: **hum sunte kaise hain?** Hawa mein chalti hui sound wave hamare sir ke andar ek electric message mein kaise badalti hai, jise dimaag \"awaaz\" samajhta hai? Aur agar kaan itna nazuk yantra hai, to bahut tez shor (noise) se uska kya hota hai? Ye chapter ka aakhri topic hai, to end mein poore chapter ka wrap-up bhi hoga.",
            "bodyHinglish": "Pichhle topic mein humne dekha ki sound ki duniya hamare sunne se kaafi badi hai. Insaan lagbhag 20 Hz se 20 kHz tak ki awaaz sun sakta hai (audible range). Usse zyada frequency wali ultrasound ko hum sun nahi paate, par chamgadad aur dolphin use sun lete hain, aur SONAR jaisi machines usse doori naapti hain. Usse kam frequency wali infrasound bhi hamare kaanon ke liye nahi hai. Topic 6 ke ant mein humne kaha tha: jo awaaz sunai nahi deti, wo bhi sound hoti hai aur uske echoes se tasveer ban sakti hai: yahi sonography ka raaz hai.\n\nAb ek sawaal bacha hai: **hum sunte kaise hain?** Hawa mein chalti hui sound wave hamare sir ke andar ek electric message mein kaise badalti hai, jise dimaag \"awaaz\" samajhta hai? Aur agar kaan itna nazuk yantra hai, to bahut tez shor (noise) se uska kya hota hai? Ye chapter ka aakhri topic hai, to end mein poore chapter ka wrap-up bhi hoga."
