            "headingHinglish": "Part C: Convex mirror: har position par ek hi kahani",
            "body": "Convex mirror mein parallel ray reflection ke baad **bikhar** jaati hai, aur peeche badhane par F (mirror ke peeche) se aati hui lagti hai. Isliye convex mirror mein reflected rays **kabhi nahi milti**. Real image banna possible hi nahi hai: sirf virtual image banti hai. Ye har position ke liye sach hai.\n\nSketch mein convex mirror \"(\" hai. F aur C mirror ke **peeche** hain (F = 10 cm, C = 20 cm peeche). Object P se 30 cm door hai.\n\n```\n                                 \\ (\n                                  \\(\n                       ↑----->-----(\n                       │ \\\\\\       (.\n                       │    \\>\\    ( .\n                       │       \\\\\\ ( .↑\n ----------------------------------(-----------\n                               /</ (\n                             //    (\n                                   (\n                                   (\n                                   P   F   C\n                       O              I\n```\n\n> **Figure 5.7** – Convex mirror: object ke top se do rays: axis ke parallel ray (reflect hokar bikharti hai, peeche badhane par F se aati lagti hai) aur P par girne wali ray. Reflected rays dotted lines peeche milti hain. Image mirror ke peeche, P aur F ke beech (yahan 7.5 cm par), chhoti, virtual aur erect.\n\nAap object ko kahin bhi rakho, ye chaaron baatein hamesha sach rehti hain: image **mirror ke peeche, P aur F ke beech, object se chhoti, virtual aur erect**.\n\n| Object ki position | Image ki position | Size | Nature |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Infinity par | F par (mirror ke peeche) | Bahut chhoti (point jaisi) | Virtual, erect |\n| Infinity aur P ke beech (kahin bhi) | P aur F ke beech (mirror ke peeche) | Chhoti (diminished) | Virtual, erect |\n\nObject jaise-jaise mirror ke kareeb aata hai, image bhi P ke kareeb aati hai aur size mein object ke paas aati jaati hai (par kabhi object se badi nahi hoti).",
            "bodyHinglish": "Convex mirror mein parallel ray reflection ke baad **bikhar** jaati hai, aur peeche badhane par F (mirror ke peeche) se aati hui lagti hai. Isliye convex mirror mein reflected rays **kabhi nahi milti**. Real image banna possible hi nahi hai: sirf virtual image banti hai. Ye har position ke liye sach hai.\n\nSketch mein convex mirror \"(\" hai. F aur C mirror ke **peeche** hain (F = 10 cm, C = 20 cm peeche). Object P se 30 cm door hai.\n\n```\n                                 \\ (\n                                  \\(\n                       ↑----->-----(\n                       │ \\\\\\       (.\n                       │    \\>\\    ( .\n                       │       \\\\\\ ( .↑\n ----------------------------------(-----------\n                               /</ (\n                             //    (\n                                   (\n                                   (\n                                   P   F   C\n                       O              I\n```\n\n> **Figure 5.7** – Convex mirror: object ke top se do rays: axis ke parallel ray (reflect hokar bikharti hai, peeche badhane par F se aati lagti hai) aur P par girne wali ray. Reflected rays dotted lines peeche milti hain. Image mirror ke peeche, P aur F ke beech (yahan 7.5 cm par), chhoti, virtual aur erect.\n\nAap object ko kahin bhi rakho, ye chaaron baatein hamesha sach rehti hain: image **mirror ke peeche, P aur F ke beech, object se chhoti, virtual aur erect**.\n\n| Object ki position | Image ki position | Size | Nature |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Infinity par | F par (mirror ke peeche) | Bahut chhoti (point jaisi) | Virtual, erect |\n| Infinity aur P ke beech (kahin bhi) | P aur F ke beech (mirror ke peeche) | Chhoti (diminished) | Virtual, erect |\n\nObject jaise-jaise mirror ke kareeb aata hai, image bhi P ke kareeb aati hai aur size mein object ke paas aati jaati hai (par kabhi object se badi nahi hoti)."
