            "heading": "Quick Recap",
            "headingHinglish": "Quick Recap",
            "body": "- **Lens** = transparent tukda jo do surfaces se ghira ho, jisme kam se kam ek spherical ho.\n- **Convex** (converging): beech mein moti. **Concave** (diverging): beech mein patli.\n- Lens ko chhote prisms ka set samjho: convex = do prisms base se base, concave = do prisms apex se apex.\n- **O** = optical centre. **Principal axis** = lens ke centres of curvature aur O se guzarti line. **C₁, C₂** = centres of curvature. **F₁, F₂** = do principal foci (O se barabar doori par). **f = OF.** **Aperture** = lens ki chaudai.\n- Convex lens ka focus **real**, concave lens ka **virtual**.\n- **Teen khaas kirnein:** (1) axis ke parallel: F₂ se guzarti (convex) ya F₁ se aati lagti (concave). (2) F₁ se guzarti (convex) ya F₂ ki taraf jaati (concave): axis ke parallel. (3) O se guzarti: seedhi nikal jaati hai.\n- **Sign convention (thoda extra, Class 10 overlap):** convex lens ki f positive, concave lens ki f negative (mirror se ulta).\n- **Sun-image activity:** lens se sharp bright spot tak ki doori ≈ f. Spot garm hota hai: savdhani rakho (burning glass).\n- Chhoti focal length wali lens zyada taqatwar (zyada tez modti) hai (power Topic 6 mein).\n- Lens kirnein guzarne deta hai, mirror wapas bhejta hai.\n- Medium badalne par lens ka behaviour badal sakta hai (aage ki class mein).",
            "bodyHinglish": "- **Lens** = transparent tukda jo do surfaces se ghira ho, jisme kam se kam ek spherical ho.\n- **Convex** (converging): beech mein moti. **Concave** (diverging): beech mein patli.\n- Lens ko chhote prisms ka set samjho: convex = do prisms base se base, concave = do prisms apex se apex.\n- **O** = optical centre. **Principal axis** = lens ke centres of curvature aur O se guzarti line. **C₁, C₂** = centres of curvature. **F₁, F₂** = do principal foci (O se barabar doori par). **f = OF.** **Aperture** = lens ki chaudai.\n- Convex lens ka focus **real**, concave lens ka **virtual**.\n- **Teen khaas kirnein:** (1) axis ke parallel: F₂ se guzarti (convex) ya F₁ se aati lagti (concave). (2) F₁ se guzarti (convex) ya F₂ ki taraf jaati (concave): axis ke parallel. (3) O se guzarti: seedhi nikal jaati hai.\n- **Sign convention (thoda extra, Class 10 overlap):** convex lens ki f positive, concave lens ki f negative (mirror se ulta).\n- **Sun-image activity:** lens se sharp bright spot tak ki doori ≈ f. Spot garm hota hai: savdhani rakho (burning glass).\n- Chhoti focal length wali lens zyada taqatwar (zyada tez modti) hai (power Topic 6 mein).\n- Lens kirnein guzarne deta hai, mirror wapas bhejta hai.\n- Medium badalne par lens ka behaviour badal sakta hai (aage ki class mein)."
