            "body": "1. A convex lens forms a sharp bright spot of the Sun on a paper, 14 cm from the lens. Estimate its focal length. How far are F₁ and F₂ from the optical centre, and what is the distance between F₁ and F₂?\n2. A convex lens has f = 15 cm. Mark F₁, F₂, 2F₁ and 2F₂ on the principal axis, giving their distances from O.\n3. Write f with its sign for: (a) a convex lens of focal length 30 cm, (b) a concave lens of focal length 12 cm, (c) a convex lens of focal length 0.4 m, (d) a concave lens of focal length 0.2 m.\n4. A beam of parallel rays falls on a lens. After refraction the rays spread out and appear to come from a point 20 cm in front of the lens. Which type of lens is it? Is its focus real or virtual? Find f with sign.\n5. Say true or false and correct if false: (a) A lens has only one focus. (b) The optical centre and the focus are the same point. (c) A ray passing through the optical centre of a thin lens bends sharply. (d) A convex lens always makes objects look bigger.\n6. A convex lens has f = 10 cm. (a) Where does a ray parallel to the axis, 2 cm above it, cross the principal axis after refraction? (b) What happens to a ray passing through F₁? (c) What happens to a ray passing through O?\n7. Two convex lenses have focal lengths 8 cm and 20 cm. Which is stronger (bends light more)? Give a one-line reason.\n8. Sort into convex or concave: (a) a magnifying glass, (b) a spectacle lens for a short-sighted person, (c) a door peephole, (d) a projector lens.\n9. A student says, \"A convex lens of f = 12 cm has its two foci 12 cm apart.\" Point out the mistake and give the correct distance.\n10. *(Thoda extra)* Why is the focal length of a convex lens taken as positive and that of a concave lens as negative in the New Cartesian sign convention?\n\n### Answers\n\n1. f ≈ **14 cm**. F₁ aur F₂ dono O se **14 cm** door hain (har taraf ek). F₁F₂ = 14 cm + 14 cm = **28 cm**.\n   Jaanch: 2 × 14 cm = 28 cm ✅\n\n2. F₁ aur F₂, O se **15 cm** door (ek-ek har taraf). 2F₁ aur 2F₂, O se 2 × 15 cm = **30 cm** door (ek-ek har taraf).\n   Jaanch: 30 cm ÷ 2 = 15 cm = f ✅\n\n3. (a) **+30 cm**. (b) **−12 cm**. (c) 0.4 m = 40 cm, f = **+40 cm**. (d) 0.2 m = 20 cm, f = **−20 cm**.\n   Jaanch: convex +, concave −. 40 cm ÷ 100 = 0.4 m ✅, 20 cm ÷ 100 = 0.2 m ✅\n\n4. Kirnein phail rahi hain, isliye **concave lens**. Focus **virtual** hai (kirnein sirf aati hui lagti hain), light ki ulti direction mein. f = **−20 cm**.\n   Jaanch: concave ki f negative ✅\n\n5. (a) **False** ❌. Lens ke do foci hote hain (F₁ aur F₂).\n   (b) **False** ❌. O lens ka beech ka point hai, F lens se f doori par axis ka point hai.\n   (c) **False** ❌. O se guzarti ray bina mude seedhi nikalti hai.\n   (d) **False** ❌. Ye cheez ki lens se doori par depend karta hai (Topic 6).\n\n6. (a) Ray F₂ se guzarti hai, isliye axis ko O se **10 cm** aage kaatti hai.\n   (b) F₁ se guzarti ray refract hokar **principal axis ke parallel** ho jaati hai.\n   (c) O se guzarti ray **seedhi nikal jaati hai**.\n   Jaanch: 10 cm = f ✅\n\n7. **8 cm** waali lens zyada taqatwar hai, kyunki jis lens ki focal length chhoti hoti hai wo kirnein ko zyada modti hai.\n   Jaanch: 8 cm < 20 cm ✅\n\n8. (a) **Convex**. (b) **Concave**. (c) **Concave**. (d) **Convex**.\n\n9. Galti: dono foci 12 cm door samajhna. Sahi: har focus O se 12 cm door hai, ek-ek har taraf, to F₁F₂ = 2 × 12 cm = **24 cm**.\n   Jaanch: 12 cm + 12 cm = 24 cm ✅\n\n10. Convex lens ka real focus F₂ light ki **same** direction mein (lens ke peeche) hai, to f positive. Concave lens ka virtual focus F₁ light ki **ulti** direction mein (lens ke aage) hai, to f negative. Light ki direction mein doori +, ulti mein −.\n\n---\n\nAb tum pehchan sakte ho ki lens convex hai ya concave, uske O, F₁, F₂, f kya hain, aur teen khaas kirnein kahan jaati hain. Yuvaan ke sawal ka pehla hissa khul gaya: ek lens kirnein ikattha karti hai, doosri phailati hai.\n\n**Aage kya?** Ab dekhte hain ki object ko lens ke kareeb ya door rakhne par image kaisi banti hai. Topic 6 mein hum in teen kirnein se ray diagram banayenge aur dekhenge ki loupe se cheez bada kyun dikhta hai, aur kab nahi.",
