            "heading": "Part C: Bijli ki safety",
            "headingHinglish": "Part C: Bijli ki safety",
            "body": "### Safety ke niyam\n\n1. **Sockets ko overload mat karo:** ek hi socket mein kai heavy appliance mat lagao (jaise geyser aur iron ek hi extension board mein).\n2. **Geele haath se ya geele farsh par nange pair se** switch, plug ya kisi appliance ko mat chhuo.\n3. **Fuse ke badle moti taar ya zyada rating ka fuse kabhi mat lagao.** Fuse ka kaam hi pighalkar circuit todna hai: moti taar lagane se wo kaam nahi karega aur wiring garam hokar aag laga sakti hai.\n4. Kisi bhi repair se pehle **switch off karo aur plug nikalo**. Repair **sirf licensed electrician** karta hai.\n5. **Ghisi hui ya katti hui taar aur dheele plug** ka istemaal mat karo.\n6. **Chhote bachon** ko sockets se door rakho: socket par **safety cover** lagao.\n7. **Patang** bijli ki lines ke paas mat udao, aur **khambe par mat chadho**.\n8. Zameen par **girey hue taar** se door raho aur turant bijli ke vibhag ko batao.\n9. **Bijli ki aag mein paani kabhi mat daalo.** Pehle supply band karo, phir **dry powder ya CO₂ extinguisher** use karo. (Ye aam salah hai; hamesha pehle apni jaan bachao aur madad bulao.)\n10. **Toofan aur bijli kadakne** mein khule maidaan, bade ped ya khambe ke paas mat khade ho (Topic 1 mein lightning ki safety dekhi thi): pakki imaarat ke andar raho.\n\n### Bijli ke jhatke par first aid (aam salah)\n\n- Peedit ko **bilkul mat chhuo** jab tak wo live taar se juda ho: tumhe bhi jhatka lag sakta hai.\n- **Sabse pehle main supply (main switch) band karo.**\n- Agar switch tak jaana mumkin na ho, to khud sookhi jagah par (jaise sookhi lakdi ya rubber mat par) khade hokar **sookhi lakdi ki lathi** se taar ko ya peedit ko door dhakel do. Koi geeli ya dhaatu ki cheez kabhi mat use karo.\n- Turant **doctor ya ambulance ko bulao** aur madad aane tak shaant rakho.\n\n### Aur kuch safety ke upkaran\n\n- **MCB:** fuse jaisa switch jo zyada current par apne aap band ho jaata hai, aur use dobara chalu kiya ja sakta hai.\n- **RCD ya ELCB:** ye wo device hai jo tab **trip** hota hai (supply kaat deta hai) jab kuch current **leak hokar earth ki taraf jaata hai**. Ye jhatke se bachane mein madad karta hai. (Sirf naam aur idea.)",
            "bodyHinglish": "### Safety ke niyam\n\n1. **Sockets ko overload mat karo:** ek hi socket mein kai heavy appliance mat lagao (jaise geyser aur iron ek hi extension board mein).\n2. **Geele haath se ya geele farsh par nange pair se** switch, plug ya kisi appliance ko mat chhuo.\n3. **Fuse ke badle moti taar ya zyada rating ka fuse kabhi mat lagao.** Fuse ka kaam hi pighalkar circuit todna hai: moti taar lagane se wo kaam nahi karega aur wiring garam hokar aag laga sakti hai.\n4. Kisi bhi repair se pehle **switch off karo aur plug nikalo**. Repair **sirf licensed electrician** karta hai.\n5. **Ghisi hui ya katti hui taar aur dheele plug** ka istemaal mat karo.\n6. **Chhote bachon** ko sockets se door rakho: socket par **safety cover** lagao.\n7. **Patang** bijli ki lines ke paas mat udao, aur **khambe par mat chadho**.\n8. Zameen par **girey hue taar** se door raho aur turant bijli ke vibhag ko batao.\n9. **Bijli ki aag mein paani kabhi mat daalo.** Pehle supply band karo, phir **dry powder ya CO₂ extinguisher** use karo. (Ye aam salah hai; hamesha pehle apni jaan bachao aur madad bulao.)\n10. **Toofan aur bijli kadakne** mein khule maidaan, bade ped ya khambe ke paas mat khade ho (Topic 1 mein lightning ki safety dekhi thi): pakki imaarat ke andar raho.\n\n### Bijli ke jhatke par first aid (aam salah)\n\n- Peedit ko **bilkul mat chhuo** jab tak wo live taar se juda ho: tumhe bhi jhatka lag sakta hai.\n- **Sabse pehle main supply (main switch) band karo.**\n- Agar switch tak jaana mumkin na ho, to khud sookhi jagah par (jaise sookhi lakdi ya rubber mat par) khade hokar **sookhi lakdi ki lathi** se taar ko ya peedit ko door dhakel do. Koi geeli ya dhaatu ki cheez kabhi mat use karo.\n- Turant **doctor ya ambulance ko bulao** aur madad aane tak shaant rakho.\n\n### Aur kuch safety ke upkaran\n\n- **MCB:** fuse jaisa switch jo zyada current par apne aap band ho jaata hai, aur use dobara chalu kiya ja sakta hai.\n- **RCD ya ELCB:** ye wo device hai jo tab **trip** hota hai (supply kaat deta hai) jab kuch current **leak hokar earth ki taraf jaata hai**. Ye jhatke se bachane mein madad karta hai. (Sirf naam aur idea.)"
