            "headingHinglish": "Jahaaz ki deck par compass",
            "body": "Ek shaam ek bada jahaaz (ship) samundar mein chal raha tha. Deck par buzurg captain Mr. Deshpande kursi par baithe the, aur unke saath ek chhota ladka Chirag tha, jo pehli baar jahaaz par aaya tha.\n\nCaptain ke saamne ek chhota sa gol compass laga hua tha, jiske andar ek patli needle thi. Jahaaz ne dheere se mod liya. Chirag ne dekha ki jahaaz ghooma, deck ghoomi, compass ka dabba bhi ghooma, par **needle apni jagah, usi disha mein tiki rahi.**\n\nChirag hairaan hua, \"Captain saab, ye needle ko kaun pakde hue hai? Jahaaz kitna bhi ghoome, ye hamesha ek hi taraf kyun dikhati hai? Kisi ne isse dhaaga to bandha nahi hai!\"\n\nMr. Deshpande muskuraye, \"Dhaaga nahi hai beta, ek **force** hai jo dikhta nahi.\"\n\nChirag ki nazar captain ke bade steel ke toolbox par padi. Usne poocha, \"Aur agar main ye bhaari steel ka toolbox compass ke bahut paas rakh doon, to kya needle tab bhi waise hi chalegi?\"\n\n\"Bahut accha sawal,\" Mr. Deshpande bole. \"Pehle ye samajh lo ki magnet ke aas-paas ka force kaise 'failta' hai. Phir tumhare dono sawalon ka jawab apne aap mil jayega.\" Is kahani ko hum Part D mein solve karenge.",
