            "heading": "Part E: Prithvi ek bada magnet hai",
            "headingHinglish": "Part E: Prithvi ek bada magnet hai",
            "body": "Compass ki needle ka N sira hamesha north ki taraf kyun jata hai? Iska jawab ye hai: **Prithvi khud ek bahut bada magnet ki tarah vyavhaar karti hai.** Maano ki Prithvi ke andar ek bahut bada bar magnet rakha ho, aur uska magnetic field poori Prithvi ke aas-paas phailta hai.\n\n```\n                      Geographic North\n                             :\n                     .-~~~~~~:~~~~~-.\n                  .-'         :  S    '-.\n        ^        /            : ║       \\        ^\n        ^       (             :║         )       ^\n        ^       (             ║:         )       ^\n        ^       (            ║ :         )       ^\n        ^        \\          N  :        /        ^\n                  '-.          :      .-'\n                     '-~~~~~~~~:~~~~-'\n                             :\n                      Geographic South\n```\n\n> **Figure 2.9** – Prithvi ke andar ka kalpanik bar magnet (axis se lagbhag 10° jhuka hua, ye angle approximate hai). Bahar ke arrows (^) field ki disha dikhate hain: zameen ke paas south se north ki taraf.\n\n### Magnetic north ek magnetic SOUTH pole hai\n\nEk dilchasp baat. Compass needle ka **N sira** Prithvi ke north ki taraf jata hai. Ye \"N sira\" ek north pole hai. Aur hum jaante hain ki **unlike poles attract karte hain** (north pole south pole ko khinchta hai). Isliye needle ka N sira Prithvi ke us pole ki taraf kheencha ja raha hai jo ek **magnetic SOUTH pole** hai.\n\nYaani Prithvi ke andar ke kalpanik bar magnet ka jo sira **geographic north ke paas** hai, wo asal mein us magnet ka **S pole** hai. (Naam \"magnetic north pole\" isliye rakha gaya ki wo north disha mein hai, par bar magnet ke hisaab se wo S pole hai.)\n\n### Magnetic poles aur geographic poles alag hain\n\n- **Geographic poles:** Prithvi ke ghoomne ke axis ke sire.\n- **Magnetic poles:** Prithvi ke magnetic field ke sire. Ye geographic poles ke **paas** hain, par **bilkul wahan nahi**. Kalpanik bar magnet ka axis ghoomne ke axis se lagbhag 10° jhuka hua hai (approximate).\n- Magnetic poles **ek jagah par fixed nahi** hain: ye dheere-dheere khiskte (wander) rehte hain.\n\n### Declination aur dip (sirf naam)\n\n- **Declination:** kisi jagah par **geographic north aur magnetic north ke beech ka kon (angle)**. Compass ka N sira magnetic north ki taraf jata hai, isliye wo geographic north se thoda alag dikhata hai. Declination alag jagahon par alag hota hai.\n- **Dip:** Prithvi ka field zameen ke saath ek khaas kon par jhukta hai: ise dip kehte hain. Ye abhi sirf naam jaan lo. (Aage ki class mein.)\n\n### Prithvi ka field aata kahan se hai? (aage ki class mein)\n\nScientists ke mutabik Prithvi ke andar, **bahari core mein pighle hue lohe (molten iron) ki gati** se ye field banta hai. Ye \"aage ki class mein\" seekhenge.\n\n### Prithvi ke field ke kaam\n\n- **Disha dhoondhna (navigation):** compass isi field ki wajah se kaam karta hai.\n- **Jaanwar:** kaha jata hai ki kai pravasi (migrating) pakshi aur samudri kachhue (turtles) lambe safar mein is field se raasta pehchante hain. Scientists ko lagta hai ki ye sahi hai, par poori tarah pakka nahi hai.\n- **Aurora:** Suraj se aane wale charged particles Prithvi ke field ki wajah se poles ke paas khinch jate hain, aur wahan aasmaan mein rangeen roshni (aurora) banti hai. (Ek line ki baat, bas jaan lo.)\n\n### Magnetic shielding\n\nKabhi kisi nazuk instrument ko bahar ke magnetic field se bachana hota hai. Iske liye us instrument ke charon taraf **naram lohe (soft iron) ka chhalla (ring)** rakhte hain. Field lines lohe ke andar se guzarti hain, aur chhalle ke andar ki jagah lagbhag field-free rehti hai. Ise **magnetic shielding** kehte hain.",
            "bodyHinglish": "Compass ki needle ka N sira hamesha north ki taraf kyun jata hai? Iska jawab ye hai: **Prithvi khud ek bahut bada magnet ki tarah vyavhaar karti hai.** Maano ki Prithvi ke andar ek bahut bada bar magnet rakha ho, aur uska magnetic field poori Prithvi ke aas-paas phailta hai.\n\n```\n                      Geographic North\n                             :\n                     .-~~~~~~:~~~~~-.\n                  .-'         :  S    '-.\n        ^        /            : ║       \\        ^\n        ^       (             :║         )       ^\n        ^       (             ║:         )       ^\n        ^       (            ║ :         )       ^\n        ^        \\          N  :        /        ^\n                  '-.          :      .-'\n                     '-~~~~~~~~:~~~~-'\n                             :\n                      Geographic South\n```\n\n> **Figure 2.9** – Prithvi ke andar ka kalpanik bar magnet (axis se lagbhag 10° jhuka hua, ye angle approximate hai). Bahar ke arrows (^) field ki disha dikhate hain: zameen ke paas south se north ki taraf.\n\n### Magnetic north ek magnetic SOUTH pole hai\n\nEk dilchasp baat. Compass needle ka **N sira** Prithvi ke north ki taraf jata hai. Ye \"N sira\" ek north pole hai. Aur hum jaante hain ki **unlike poles attract karte hain** (north pole south pole ko khinchta hai). Isliye needle ka N sira Prithvi ke us pole ki taraf kheencha ja raha hai jo ek **magnetic SOUTH pole** hai.\n\nYaani Prithvi ke andar ke kalpanik bar magnet ka jo sira **geographic north ke paas** hai, wo asal mein us magnet ka **S pole** hai. (Naam \"magnetic north pole\" isliye rakha gaya ki wo north disha mein hai, par bar magnet ke hisaab se wo S pole hai.)\n\n### Magnetic poles aur geographic poles alag hain\n\n- **Geographic poles:** Prithvi ke ghoomne ke axis ke sire.\n- **Magnetic poles:** Prithvi ke magnetic field ke sire. Ye geographic poles ke **paas** hain, par **bilkul wahan nahi**. Kalpanik bar magnet ka axis ghoomne ke axis se lagbhag 10° jhuka hua hai (approximate).\n- Magnetic poles **ek jagah par fixed nahi** hain: ye dheere-dheere khiskte (wander) rehte hain.\n\n### Declination aur dip (sirf naam)\n\n- **Declination:** kisi jagah par **geographic north aur magnetic north ke beech ka kon (angle)**. Compass ka N sira magnetic north ki taraf jata hai, isliye wo geographic north se thoda alag dikhata hai. Declination alag jagahon par alag hota hai.\n- **Dip:** Prithvi ka field zameen ke saath ek khaas kon par jhukta hai: ise dip kehte hain. Ye abhi sirf naam jaan lo. (Aage ki class mein.)\n\n### Prithvi ka field aata kahan se hai? (aage ki class mein)\n\nScientists ke mutabik Prithvi ke andar, **bahari core mein pighle hue lohe (molten iron) ki gati** se ye field banta hai. Ye \"aage ki class mein\" seekhenge.\n\n### Prithvi ke field ke kaam\n\n- **Disha dhoondhna (navigation):** compass isi field ki wajah se kaam karta hai.\n- **Jaanwar:** kaha jata hai ki kai pravasi (migrating) pakshi aur samudri kachhue (turtles) lambe safar mein is field se raasta pehchante hain. Scientists ko lagta hai ki ye sahi hai, par poori tarah pakka nahi hai.\n- **Aurora:** Suraj se aane wale charged particles Prithvi ke field ki wajah se poles ke paas khinch jate hain, aur wahan aasmaan mein rangeen roshni (aurora) banti hai. (Ek line ki baat, bas jaan lo.)\n\n### Magnetic shielding\n\nKabhi kisi nazuk instrument ko bahar ke magnetic field se bachana hota hai. Iske liye us instrument ke charon taraf **naram lohe (soft iron) ka chhalla (ring)** rakhte hain. Field lines lohe ke andar se guzarti hain, aur chhalle ke andar ki jagah lagbhag field-free rehti hai. Ise **magnetic shielding** kehte hain."
