            "heading": "Part F: Solved examples",
            "headingHinglish": "Part F: Solved examples",
            "body": "**Example 1 (compass ki disha, 6 jagah):** Neeche bar magnet ke aas-paas 6 jagahon par chhota compass rakha hai. Har jagah needle ke **N sire** ki disha batao. (Bar magnet ka N bayein taraf hai.)\n\n```\n           5      1\n           ·      ·\n\n     3 ·  [N═════════════S] · 4\n\n                  ·      ·\n                  2      6\n```\n\n> **Figure 2.10** – Bar magnet ke aas-paas compass ki 6 jagah (1 aur 2 beech ke upar aur neeche, 3 N ke bayein, 4 S ke daayein, 5 N ke upar, 6 S ke neeche).\n\nRule: needle ka N sira field ki disha mein point karta hai, aur bahar field N se S ki taraf jaati hai.\n\n- **Jagah 1 (beech ke upar):** magnet ke N se dhakka (daayein), S ki taraf khinchav (daayein): needle **daayein (→)**.\n- **Jagah 2 (beech ke neeche):** wahi: **daayein (→)**.\n- **Jagah 3 (N ke bayein, axis par):** N se door dhakka: **bayein (←)**.\n- **Jagah 4 (S ke daayein, axis par):** S ki taraf khinchav, yaani **bayein (←)**.\n- **Jagah 5 (N ke thik upar):** N se door: **upar (↑)** (lagbhag).\n- **Jagah 6 (S ke thik neeche):** S ki taraf: **upar (↑)** (lagbhag).\n\n**Jaanch:** Jagah 1, 2: field line magnet ke beech N se S ki taraf, yaani → ✅. Jagah 3: line N se bayein nikalti hai ✅. Jagah 4: line S mein daayein se ghusti hai, yaani ← ✅\n\n**Example 2 (do magnets ke beech field ki disha):** Do bar magnets seedhi line mein hain, beech mein thodi jagah. Bayein magnet ko L, daayein ko R kaho. Beech ke bindu par compass ka N sira kis taraf jayega?\n\n- **(i) N-S** (L ka daayein sira N, R ka bayein sira S): field N se S tak: **daayein (→)**.\n- **(ii) S-N** (L ka daayein sira S, R ka bayein sira N): field R ke N se L ke S tak: **bayein (←)**.\n- **(iii) N-N:** beech ke bindu par field **zero (neutral point)**; usse bayein (L ke N ke paas) field L ke N se door, yaani **daayein (→)**; usse daayein (R ke N ke paas) **bayein (←)** (dono taraf ki lines N se door, neutral point ki taraf aakar mud jati hain).\n- **(iv) S-S:** beech mein neutral point; usse bayein (L ke S ke paas) field L ke S ki taraf, yaani **bayein (←)**; usse daayein **daayein (→)** (lines dono S ki taraf jati hain).\n\n**Jaanch:** Unlike arrangement (i, ii) mein field N se S ki taraf ✅. Like arrangement (iii, iv) mein beech ka bindu field-free ✅\n\n**Example 3 (kahan field zyada?):** Bindu P bar magnet ke N pole ke bahut paas hai, jahan lines paas-paas hain. Bindu Q magnet se door hai, jahan lines door-door hain. Kahan field zyada hai?\n\n- Jahan lines paas-paas, wahan field zyada. **P par field zyada** hai.\n\n**Jaanch:** Poles ke paas lohe ki pins sabse zyada chipakti hain: wahan field sabse zyada ✅\n\n**Example 4 (lines ginna):** Ek jaisi chhoti window P (N pole ke paas) aur Q (door) par rakhi hai. Kitni lines guzarti hain? Kahan field zyada?\n\n```\n Window P (pole ke paas)          Window Q (magnet se door)\n ┌─────────────────┐              ┌─────────────────┐\n │ ───────────>    │              │                 │\n │ ───────────>    │              │ ───────────>    │\n │ ───────────>    │              │                 │\n │ ───────────>    │              │ ───────────>    │\n │ ───────────>    │              │                 │\n └─────────────────┘              └─────────────────┘\n```\n\n> **Figure 2.11** – Same size ki window mein P par 5 lines, Q par 2 lines.\n\nP par 5 lines, Q par 2 lines. P par field **zyada**. Anuman: 5 ÷ 2 = 2.5, yaani P par field Q se lagbhag **2.5 guna** (sirf sketch ka anuman).\n\n**Jaanch:** 5 ÷ 2 = 2.5 ✅ aur 2 × 2.5 = 5 ✅\n\n**Example 5 (sketch poora karo):** Bar magnet ke upar 3 lines (a, b, c) bani hain, par arrowheads nahi lage. Kahan, kis taraf lagenge?\n\n```\n                   ------a------\n                 ~~-           --~\n                ~~       b       ~~\n                (   -----------   ~\n               (  ~~-         -~~  )\n               (~~~  ----c----  ~~))\n                ~(~---       ----~~\n                [N═══════════════S]\n```\n\n> **Figure 2.12** – Teen lines bina arrowhead ke; N bayein, S daayein.\n\nTeeno lines **N se S ki taraf**: upar a, b, c ke beech mein arrow **bayein se daayein (→)**. Bayein side par arrow **upar (^)**, daayein side par arrow **neeche (v)**.\n\n**Jaanch:** Bahar har line N (bayein) se S (daayein) ki taraf ✅\n\n**Example 6 (steel toolbox ke paas compass):** Compass ke bahut paas bada steel ka box rakha hai. Needle kya karegi?\n\n- Steel magnetic material hai: needle ka chhota magnet use khinchta hai, to needle **toolbox ki taraf ghoom jati hai**, north se hat kar.\n- Agar box khud ek **magnet** ho: uska nazdeeki pole **S** ho to needle ka **N sira** us ki taraf; nazdeeki pole **N** ho to needle ka **S sira** us ki taraf point karega.\n\n**Jaanch:** Unlike poles attract: needle ka N sira box ke S ko, S sira box ke N ko khinchta hai ✅\n\n**Example 7 (horseshoe ke beech compass):** Horseshoe magnet ke bayein arm par N, daayein par S hai. Beech mein rakhe compass ka N sira kis taraf?\n\n- Field N se S ki taraf: needle ka N sira **daayein (→)**, S arm ki taraf.\n\n**Jaanch:** Needle ka N sira S pole ki taraf khincha jata hai ✅\n\n**Example 8 (Prithvi ka sawal):** Compass needle ka N sira north ki taraf kyun jata hai? Prithvi ke north ki taraf ka magnetic pole kaisa hai?\n\n- N sira ek north pole hai. Unlike poles khinchte hain, isliye wo Prithvi ke ek **magnetic S pole** ki taraf khincha ja raha hai.\n- Isliye Prithvi ke north ke paas ka magnetic pole, kalpanik bar magnet ka **S pole** hai (naam magnetic \"north\" hai, par bar magnet ke hisaab se wo S hai).\n\n**Jaanch:** N-end north ki taraf aur N ko S khinchta hai, to north ke paas S pole ✅\n\n**Example 9 (declination ke saath):** Sign rule (sirf is example ke liye): declination 3° **East** matlab magnetic north, geographic north se 3° east mein hai. Compass angle magnetic north se naapta hai (clockwise). Ek jagah ka true bearing 90° (east) hai. Compass kitna padhega?\n\n- East wali disha magnetic north se 90° − 3° = **87°** par hai: compass **87°** dikhayega.\n- Declination 3° **West** hota, to compass 90° + 3° = **93°**.\n- Dono padhne ka antar: 93° − 87° = **6°** (= 2 × 3°).\n\n**Jaanch:** East ke liye true = compass + 3° = 87° + 3° = 90° ✅. West ke liye true = compass − 3° = 93° − 3° = 90° ✅\n\n**Example 10 (jahaaz ka heading):** Jahaaz ka compass 150° padhta hai. Declination 3° West. True heading?\n\n- West: true = compass − 3° = 150° − 3° = **147°**.\n- East hota: true = 150° + 3° = **153°**.\n\n**Jaanch:** West: 147° + 3° = 150° ✅. East: 153° − 3° = 150° ✅",
